      "y": 28,
      "text": "Let's build a sequencer, step-by-step. We can use a sawtooth oscillator to generate a tone. The sound level is controlled by an attack/decay envelope. The oscillator's output is connected to the envelope's amplitude jack so that they will be multiplied.\n\nThe lineOut connects the sound to the speakers.\n\nTo Do:\n* Click the \"trigger\" button to make the envelope go up then down in volume.\n* Click on the knob and drag up and down to change the oscillator frequency. \n* Click the \"trigger\" again to hear the new frequency.\n",
